I mostly play on a Psion Netbook. On the Psion (as with laptops) you have 
up/down/left/right arrows but not diagonals, so when I did the Psion port I 
made the 'fn' key act as a special sort of shift on the arrow keys to 
rotate them 45 degrees clockwise. i.e. up arrow becomes up+left, right 
arrow becomes right+down &c.

On Windows I mostly use a laptop, and I've become so used to the way I do 
things on the Psion that I've added similar functionality to the windows 
version but using the left-control key to rotate the arrows. Normally on 
the windows version the control key scrolls the map, so I left this 
functionality on the right control key. I also did the same for the console 
version, only there I used the Alt key so the patch doesn't actually affect 
any existing key combinations (using Alt for the windows version wouldn't 
be impossible but wouldn't be quite so trivial to program).

Its a bit idiosyncratic, but if anyone wants to try this I'm happy to post 
the patch.

